l  it was a bucket list item  and it was at you know the final five  i'm so happy for you that you got to  have that moment because there's nothing  quite like it um so if we fast forward  to that tribal council  you give your idol to marianne so can  you tell us more about that decision  well the decision was not that hard to  me because  um  lindsay had wanted the idol to save her  but lindsay had  was wasn't an alliance with omar alma  was trying to get me out with the  nullifier i love lindsay as a person but  that that point of the game i really  felt that lindsay was gonna be our  biggest competition going in into the  finals so  i couldn't give it to her and  maybe i'm using it for a reason but she  never told me about almost nullified  which proved to me she was loyal to omar  and not me  on the other side of the coins i went to  marianne to help me vote omar out and i  proved that by you utilizing the  nullifier and i promised marianne if she  did work with me i would give her my  idol i thought that would accomplish two  things it would it would show that the  jury that i was trying to be honorable  and keep my word also i really felt  it didn't matter marion wasn't on the  chopping block it was either going to be  lindsay or jonathan giving it to her  made a  a jury move and a move of loyalty to  marian where she knew that i was on her  side so it was quite easy i never  thought  other than to give it to her  so later in the episode you had another  wonderful moment the fire making  challenge and for someone who makes a  living of putting fires out the fire you  made was huge so how confident were you  going into the fire making challenge i  knew i could make fire  but as in anything in life nothing's a  sure thing jonathan was the fire beast  throughout the season he made every fire  at camp everyone's oh we get jonathan to  make the fight jonathan's great at this  jonathan's great at that and jonathan  was also very confident and as you see  through the