d beast being  deceptive if you don't do that you can't  win  my mistake was i thought that was a  given i shouldn't have and i based my  game on honor and integrity and they  pointed out some of those flaws which  ultimately hurt me  mm-hmm  you're right as you know it's tough  being in there coming at you coming at  you coming at you  because it's hours people the viewers  don't realize you're sitting there for  hours so i have respect for anyone who  is able to sit through that  yes you know how long it is we're there  for a long time  and  and and god bless the juries they they  take their they take their role very  seriously and if they feel they have a  point they're going to keep pounding  again until you either submit or you  admit to it  a hundred percent it's it's a weird part  of the game where you have these  relationships with people but you have  to accept that they're going to ask you  tough questions um and i think that what  made watching you so great is you really  invested in building relationships with  people you had a lot of open and genuine  conversations so  what do you feel like you personally are  taking away from your survivor  experience  the biggest thing i can say i take away  from my experience is getting to know  people  whether they were older  different cultures  learning how they lived and  appreciating it respecting it  and realizing  i'm a guy from jersey  johnson's a guy from alabama marian's a  girl from canada  um romeo is a guy and as different as we  really all are whether it be how we look  what religions we're all kind of the  same and i've agree i've created  friendships i have for the rest of my  life from people from all walks of life  just because i stood i took the time to  understand where they were coming from  and quite frankly they did the same for  me because i'm at face value they may  look at me and say i could never be a  friend with this guy he doesn't look  like but once they got to know me they  realized i'